## NON-NEGOTIABLE PRINCIPLES
1. ZERO-UPLOAD CORE: every studio, tool and preset processes files 100% inside the user's
   browser (WebAssembly, Web Workers, Canvas/WebGL, OPFS/IndexedDB). User files, previews
   and outputs never leave the device. No file or file metadata ever reaches any server.
2. MINIMAL CONTROL PLANE: a thin edge backend exists ONLY for accounts, sessions, sign-in,
   plans and entitlements, pricing and offers, payment webhooks, gated delivery of paid tool
   bundles, admin console data, audit logs and the secrets vault. It stores zero user files.
   Be honest with me: payment confirmation, plan enforcement, sign-in, pricing, hidden admin
   login and account erasure cannot be made secure with browser code alone. Explain this in Phase 1.
3. CLOUDFLARE FREE PLAN ONLY: everything deploys on Cloudflare's free tier from GitHub. Before
   choosing services, verify the CURRENT free-plan limits (requests per day, CPU time per
   request, database size, storage, build count), list each with a risk note, and do not
   assume limits from memory.
4. FREE & OPEN SOURCE ONLY: every library must be OSS with a permissive license. Provide a
   table: name, license, purpose, free-tier impact, alternative.
5. HIDDEN TECHNICAL DETAILS: users and guests see only short, plain-language labels and
   messages about what they can do. They never see how the platform works: no technology,
   library or service names, versions, "powered by" text, architecture, security or
   processing explanations, stack traces or raw error codes. Errors shown to users are
   plain-language with a short reference ID only. No source maps in production, and no
   technical comments or debug output in the public bundle. All technical information is
   visible ONLY to eligible admins inside the admin console (Section R), limited to what
   their role needs. Legally required notices (privacy, terms, consent) and the plain
   currency note at signup stay, written in simple user language.
6. PAID MEANS CONFIRMED: no paid/plan feature is usable until the payment gateway's webhook
   has confirmed payment and the server has marked the plan ACTIVE (Section E and Section P).
7. NO SECRETS IN DEVELOPMENT: zero real APIs, keys, tokens, client IDs or credentials in code,
   comments, seeds, env examples, CI logs, commits or UI. Use mock adapters (payments, social
   sign-in, email, SMS, storage) and clearly marked fake fixtures. Add secret-scanning and a
   pre-commit check to block accidental commits.
8. NO HARDCODED ACCOUNTS: no user/admin/super-user credentials anywhere in code or docs.
9. WORKFLOW: ask category by category (max 6 questions per message), offer a recommended
   default I can accept by replying "default", keep a Decision Log, and wait for "APPROVED"
   after each phase. If a request is impossible or unsafe, say so and propose the correct method.
10. NO LOCATION OR CURRENCY DETECTION: no IP, geolocation, browser-locale or other automatic
    region/currency detection, and no currency selector anywhere. Currency is fixed once at
    signup from the country code (Section C).
11. NEUTRAL VISUALS AND NAMES: follow Section D (no personal or AI portraits, no real
    person/place/thing names in sample content, original drawn/animated visuals only).

