## SECTION E: ENTITLEMENT ENFORCEMENT (PAID FEATURES ONLY AFTER CONFIRMED ACTIVE PLAN)
- Plan states: NONE → PENDING (order created) → ACTIVE (webhook verified) → GRACE (optional) →
  EXPIRED / CANCELLED / REFUNDED / REVOKED. Only ACTIVE (and GRACE if I approve it) unlocks
  paid features. PENDING never unlocks anything.
- Gated delivery: paid tools, presets and export modules are separate bundles NOT in the
  public app. The control plane serves them only to a signed-in user whose plan is ACTIVE,
  using short-lived signed access tokens bound to the user and session, with expiry matching
  the plan validity.
- Server-side checks: every paid-bundle request and every token refresh re-checks plan state.
  Expiry, refund, cancellation or admin revoke blocks further downloads and refresh immediately.
- Client-side checks are for UX only (locked/unlocked display), never for security.
- Anti-sharing: limit concurrent sessions/devices per plan, bind tokens to the account, flag
  abnormal token reuse for admin review.
- Be honest with me: once a paid bundle is delivered to an entitled user's browser, a
  determined user can keep that copy until the token or cache expires. Propose mitigations
  (short token lifetimes, no long offline caching for per-day passes, re-validation at each
  session start) and list the residual risk per plan in Phase 1.
- Guest and freemium limits use server-issued counters or signed allowances where possible,
  with an honest note on what can still be bypassed.
- Admin override: eligible admins can grant, extend or revoke a plan (reason, MFA re-auth,
  audit entry); the Super User can do everything.
- Testing: prove that a free user, a PENDING user, an expired user and a refunded user can NOT
  open any paid tool, even by calling the paid URLs directly.

