## SECTION K: KEYS & ENVIRONMENT GUIDED SETUP (GUIDE ME THROUGHOUT)
- TWO TIERS:
  - Tier 1, deployment secrets (needed for the control plane itself): vault master key,
    token-signing keys, session secret. I generate them locally using a command you give me,
    and set them in Cloudflare (dashboard or CLI), never in Git.
  - Tier 2, integration keys: payment gateway keys and webhook secret, Google/Apple/X
    credentials, email and SMS provider keys. An eligible admin adds them through the vault
    (Section S), starting in test mode.
- DEPLOYABILITY RULES: the app builds and deploys with no secrets; missing keys put the
  related feature into a safe "not configured" state (hidden or disabled, mock in
  development); config files contain only binding names; a names-only `.env.example`
  documents required variables; local secret files are git-ignored and secret-scanned.
  Prefer Cloudflare's direct Git integration so no Cloudflare token needs to live in GitHub;
  if a deploy token is ever needed, use a least-privilege GitHub encrypted secret.
- GUIDE FORMAT: walk me through ONE key at a time and wait for my confirmation. For each key
  give: purpose, where to obtain it, cost, exactly where to enter it, how to verify it works
  (admin-only integration check in test mode), how to rotate or revoke it, and what stays
  disabled without it. Verify current dashboard steps from official docs before instructing me.
- SAFETY: never ask me to paste a real key in chat. I enter keys only in the Cloudflare
  dashboard/CLI or the admin vault. If a key is ever exposed, guide me to revoke and rotate it.
- ORDER: (1) 2FA on GitHub and Cloudflare → (2) connect repos and deploy with zero secrets →
  (3) Tier 1 secrets → (4) bootstrap the Super User, credentials shown only in chat →
  (5) payment test keys and webhook registration → (6) social providers → (7) email/SMS
  providers → (8) full test run → (9) switch to live keys → (10) rollback rehearsal.

